  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Address the issue where tests that have an xfail marker added (using request.node.add_marker) do not behave as expected in pytest 6. In pytest 5.x, adding an xfail marker to a test caused a failing test to be treated as expected (xfail), but in pytest 6 this behavior is broken. This feature requires restoring the intended behavior by refining how xfail and skip markers are evaluated during the test setup phase. The solution must ensure that the test outcome for statically and dynamically marked tests remains consistent with the behavior of pytest 5.x.",
    "hint_texts": "This part involves refactoring and optimizing the current logic in pytest_runtest_setup and the initial section of pytest_runtest_call. Developers should focus on updating the evaluation and storage of the xfail and skip markers in the item._store data structure. The improvements should ensure that markers like xfail and skip are processed in a clean, consolidated manner without introducing regressions in the existing static marker handling.",
    "entrypoint": "Modify the file src/_pytest/skipping.py. In particular, update the functions pytest_runtest_setup and the first part of pytest_runtest_call (before the yield) where the evaluation of the skip marks and xfail marks occurs. Key modifications include changing the assignment to item._store[skipped_by_mark_key] (e.g., using 'skipped is not None') and adjusting the conditions under which xfail is triggered, especially in relation to the item.config.option.runxfail flag. Developers should begin their work around the changes near line 231 and throughout the affected blocks in that file.",
