  "feature2": {
    "prompt": "Improve the handling for cases where an xfail marker is added to a test during its execution. In the current pytest 6 implementation, dynamically added xfail markers do not cause the test to be treated as an expected failure, resulting in erroneous test outcomes. The fix should detect markers added at runtime and correctly process them so that tests dynamically flagged as xfail behave as intended, in line with the behavior in pytest 5.x. This will ensure that test results are consistent regardless of whether the marker is added statically or during execution.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature requires adding new logic to handle xfail markers that are applied dynamically during the test run. The implementation should focus on evaluating the marker state after the test call (post-yield) within pytest_runtest_call, ensuring that any dynamically added xfail markers are detected and their intended behavior enforced. Developers should design this addition to work seamlessly with the refactored marker evaluation logic from feature1.",
    "entrypoint": "Modify the file src/_pytest/skipping.py in the pytest_runtest_call function, specifically after the yield statement where the dynamic re-evaluation of xfail markers is performed. Additionally, review the modifications in the test file testing/test_skipping.py to understand how dynamic xfail markers are being tested. The starting point should be the code block added near the end of pytest_runtest_call that reassigns the xfail state, ensuring that it correctly interacts with the updated logic from feature1.",
